ternship at a fictional learning organization. Built a task management module with filtering by assignee, status and due date. Used Git branches and pull requests to keep changes small and reviewable. Added integration tests against a disposable PostgreSQL database and corrected timezone handling for task deadlines. Investigated duplicate submissions and introduced an idempotency key for one create endpoint. Compared expected and actual responses with Postman and described reproduction steps in issue reports. Worked with a mentor to understand transactions, indexes and common HTTP error codes. Wrote a short onboarding guide explaining local setup, sample data and how to run the focused tests.","company_name":"Example Learning Studio (fictional)","job_title":"Backend Intern"}],"education":[{"degree":"Bachelor of Software Engineering","start_date":"2020-09-01","end_date":"2024-06-01","description":"Completed a fictional Bachelor of Software Engineering program in 2024. Coursework covered object oriented programming, relational database design, software testing, basic computer networks and team delivery. The final project emphasized written requirements, API design, data integrity and peer review. No professional certification is claimed. Reads English technical documentation and can explain a familiar implementation in a short written summary.","school_name":"Example Engineering College (fictional)","major":"Software Engineering"}],"skills":[{"name":"Java","proficiency_level":"INTERMEDIATE"},{"name":"Spring Boot","proficiency_level":"INTERMEDIATE"},{"name":"PostgreSQL","proficiency_level":"INTERMEDIATE"},{"name":"JUnit","proficiency_level":"INTERMEDIATE"},{"name":"Docker","proficiency_level":"BASIC"},{"name":"Git","proficiency_level":"INTERMEDIATE"}],"projects":[{"role":"Backend developer","description":"Built a capstone appointment booking service with three other students. Owned backend endpoints for available slots, booking confirmation and cancellation. Prevented double booking with a database uniqueness rule and a transaction rather than a browser-only check. Implemented access and refresh token flows for a demonstration account system. Kept configuration in environment variables and excluded secrets from version control. Containerized the application and database for reproducible local demonstrations. Created sample fixtures for overlapping bookings and permission boundaries. Measured response time with a synthetic dataset and recorded the environment used; the result was a classroom demonstration rather than a production capacity benchmark. Helped write the final API handbook and showed teammates how to reproduce a failed test. Redis was used only for an optional short-lived cache; the database remained authoritative.","technologies":["Java","Spring Boot","PostgreSQL","Redis","Docker"],"project_name":"Appointment Booking Capstone (fictional)"}],"certifications":[]}
